stateDiagram-v2
    state "Tenancy -- who names the record" as rec_disc_tenancy {
        [*] --> rec_disc_owned
        rec_disc_owned --> rec_disc_orphaned : the last naming roadmap row closes
        rec_disc_orphaned --> rec_disc_owned : an open row takes the record over
    }
    state "Enquiry -- what the record has established" as rec_disc_enquiry {
        [*] --> rec_disc_open
        rec_disc_open --> rec_disc_ended : the result lands
    }
    rec_disc_open --> rec_disc_retired : the file is deleted
    rec_disc_ended --> rec_disc_retired : the file is deleted
    rec_disc_retired --> [*]
    note right of rec_disc_tenancy
        The regions are orthogonal: tenancy moves when a roadmap row opens or closes, the enquiry moves when the evidence lands. Deletion fires while the tenancy is orphaned, or when the record fails a criterion its review applies, whatever the enquiry has established.
    end note
